# Line endings, settled once.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# Without it, 29 files showed as modified having had nothing done to them:
# 188 insertions and 188 deletions across four files, every line "changed",
# and `git diff --ignore-all-space` showing zero actual differences. The
# files were written to disk with CRLF while the repo held LF, and with
# core.autocrlf unset git treats that as real content.
#
# That is worse than cosmetic. A diff where every line changed hides the
# one line that actually did, and this project's whole debugging method
# has been reading diffs carefully.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, stores it with LF in
# the repository, and checks it out with LF. The deployed dashboard runs on
# Linux, so LF everywhere also means the file on Streamlit Cloud is
# byte-identical to the file on this machine.
#
# Python, pandas and every editor worth using handle LF on Windows without
# complaint. If some tool ever does complain, the fix is to give that one
# file its own rule below -- not to turn this off.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary, so git never tries to normalise or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.joblib binary
*.pkl binary
*.parquet binary
